course: dictionary
lesson: 12597
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «discharged» is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they give you clues. «Mia was discharged from hospital on Monday.» The words hospital and home tell you that Mia was allowed to leave and go home.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «The torch did not work because its battery was discharged.» The clue is that the torch did not work. A discharged battery has used up its stored electricity, so it has no power left.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense. «Waste was discharged into the river» works with «let out» or «flowed out», so you know it means poured out.
fact: Discharged is the past form of discharge: discharge, discharges, discharged, discharging.
fact: «Discharged» can mean allowed to go home from hospital.
fact: «Discharged» can mean officially allowed or made to leave the army or a job.
fact: «Discharged» can mean that a battery has used up its stored electricity, or that a liquid or gas was let out or flowed out.
fact: «Discharged» can also mean fired, as with a gun, or done or paid, as with a duty or debt, which is a more formal use.
exercise: «Mia was discharged from hospital on Monday.» What does discharged mean here? | Given a new name | *Allowed to go home | Fired from a job | Sent to sleep
exercise: «The torch did not work because its battery was discharged.» What does discharged mean? | *Its stored electricity had been used up | It was covered in water | It was cleaned and polished | Its stored electricity had been made bigger
exercise: «Waste was discharged into the river.» What does discharged mean? | *Let out and flowed out | Frozen solid | Gently rubbed clean | Stored safely in a box
test: «After the soldier was discharged from the army, he became a teacher.» What does discharged mean here? | Trained for a new job | Given a medal | *Officially allowed or made to leave | Sent to sleep
test: «The doctor said the debt had been discharged.» In this formal sense, what does discharged mean? | Lost | Cut into pieces | *Paid in full | Put on a shelf
exam: «The nurse said the patient would be discharged tomorrow.» What does discharged mean? | Sent to a different ward | *Allowed to go home | Given a bath | Painted green
